<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Nafin lowers Jan credit rate to 32.25 pct.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Nafin lowers Jan credit rate to 32.25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state development bank Nacional Financiera (Nafin) said Thursday it lowered its peso-denominated credit rate in January to 32.25 percent.</p>
<p>The rate, known as the Tasa Nafin, is 250 basis points below the December level, Nafin said.</p>
<p>The Tasa Nafin is the rate set by the bank for credits and refinancings for small and medium-sized businesses in Mexico.</p>
<p>((-- Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
